"What may differ between BN5's battle (the reference) and BN6's with a family moved in (the subject), and why: tools/xdiff.py reads each game's numbers as BN6's (maps), each game's structures through their own layouts (layouts), and replays BN6's draws from BN5's by the twins of its rng, the engine's own draws one game alone makes named there too (rng), and lets a difference pass only where a mask names it (masks), each an engine difference that is not the family's code, with the evidence: both games' routines by address. No mask applies to the family's own records (its objects, what they own, its attacks and effects): what the engine writes there in its own numbers is read as BN6's in the snapshot, as an enemy id is (maps: alliance, renderer, slot), and any other difference there fails the spec (docs/multirom/families.md; docs/devtools/differential.md). No game code here: addresses and numbers only."
